/*
*/
Rationalisation are used to "resolve" traumatic events that otherwise would occasionally add more stress/trauma.
Traumatic events would be diary entries that have recorded high trauma increase
  That would mean depending on traits and insecurities some minor events might end up producing high trauma
  Could have importance treshold for an event to be traumatic, 2 probably but the issue with that is importance customisation is a thing so would mean tracking the default importance or disabling importance customisation until the entry is being written.
  It's mostly the case already but making sure that there isn't more than 1 normal diary entry per event would be more important so that trauma doesn't get split up causing otherwise traumatic event to not count as one.
    Or could just have all events that give even a bit of trauma count and have some method for player to combine them into one entry.!


For nice rationalisations there probably needs to be at least some understanding of what the event was ie. Did you successfully resist/escape(and did you even try to)? Did it have an aggressor whose behaviour can be given explanation?
But how far can we get with rationalisations that don't care about what the situation and can be equally applied to any situation.
seeing someone get treated badly, beating up an attacker and having sex
  masturbating in a temple as an angel(+50)
  thinking you are going to get crushed by a trash compactor (+24)
  Being forcibly milked while not cow transformed(+24)
  bracing for it while being branded(+18)
  having your penis size announced(+15 or +10)
  failing to complete a slime task(+12)
  having people throw stones at you while you are bound and naked(+12)
  reading a terrible scroll(+12)
  having Kylar break down in tears after you refuse to let him rape you(+12)
  escaping a beast(+12)
  Having police strip you in a street and try to remove your chastity by electrocuting you(+10)
  being seen orgasming in public while embarrased about public nudity(+10)
  Reaching max stress while sleeping(+10)

General rationalisations(and potential effects):
Hopefully more happiness was gained than lost
  
Fight against the corruption requires sacrifices
Everything happens for a reason/It was meant to be/
  just % reduction in trauma?
I need the money/
  Reduce trauma based on money gained
I deserved that/
  could require one of:
	A. Allure higher than necessary
	B. Being out at night
	C. Seduction attempt
	D. Crime increase
	or it could just always be an option
  
Everything can be learning experience
World is cruel
What doesn't kill you makes you stronger
Strong deserve to rule over the weak
I've experienced worse/


What effects should there be?
Trauma reduced based on:
  arousal gain
  fame gain
  fluids gotten on body

Actually checking the entry for arousalgain and such is pretty neat and might mean not needing tags or such for events at all, checking for famescrap should inform if the fight was a loss and gaining some sort of rapestat would mean something you didn't consent(though there are probably some edge cases), could add some new stats if they aren't enough, like is famescrap reliable way to tell you reduced enemyhealth to 0?
  

:: Rationalisation Widgets [widget]
/*

How should the interface for picking a rationalisation work?
Diary entry + rationalisation options as links(each having it's own line and potentially followed by stuff indicating/explaining what effect it has) sounds best for now. 
Dropdown menu, radiobutton or checkbox or such don't sound that great.
	For rationalisation selection that sounds fine but there's also writing non traumatic entries and with how many of them there usually will be going through them 1 by 1 seems like a pain, check boxes for entries you want to keep seems like a decent option, will just need good options for what to pick by default, something like importance 3+ or money gained.
	Rationalisation selection could happen after you've picked events to write, traumatic events you don't pick could just remain in the list until you pick them instead of being removed/compressed like other events. 


Should I start off by making most rationalisations just resolve the trauma from event and do nothing else(with one or two that are always available but give trauma when used)? Idea being that it's a matter of having one that you can use... Maybe but it feels like it'd need something more at some point but as a starting point it doesn't seem bad.

Once you do pick a rationalisation where and how should I save that?
Adding it to $log... wait, to $diary I mean seems natural but since not all entries will have one not defining the property might be good, just need to make sure that that's handled properly.
As for how, could go with just a number but number and a string might be better

*/



<<widget "pickrationalisation">><<nobr>>
<<if ndef $rationalisation>>
	<<rationaliseinit>>
<</if>>
<!-- This needs capture doesn't it? -->
<<run console.log("Rationalising event "+$args[1]+" of log page "+$args[0]+"(day"+$log[$args[0]][$args[1]][$logpars.day]+").")>>
<<run console.log("In diary the event is day"+$diary["day"+$log[$args[0]][$args[1]][$logpars.day]].day+", entry "+($diary["day"+$log[$args[0]][$args[1]][$logpars.day]].entries.length-1)+".")>>
<<set _day to $log[$args[0]][$args[1]][$logpars.day]>>
<<set $entryid to $diary["day"+$log[$args[0]][$args[1]][$logpars.day]].entries.length - 1>><!-- Assuming that we're rationalising the last entry added to $diary, might need to not do that at some point -->
<<capture _day $entryid>>

<<if $rationalisation.deserve isnot undefined>>
	<<link [[I deserved that|$passage]]>>
		<!--<<rationalise>>-->
		<<set $diary["day"+$log[$args[0]][$args[1]][$logpars.day]].entries[$entryid][3] to "I deserved that.">>
		<<set $ratiid += 1>>
		<!--<<trauma 1>>-->
	<</link>><!--<<gtrauma>>-->
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if $rationalisation.polite isnot undefined>>
	<<if $log[$args[0]][$args[1]][$logpars.stats].submissivegain lte -1>>
		<<link [[Politeness is important|$passage]]>>
			<<set $diary["day"+$log[$args[0]][$args[1]][$logpars.day]].entries[$entryid][3] to "Politeness is important.">>
			<<trauma -2>>
			<<set $ratiid += 1>>
		<</link>><<ltrauma>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<<if $rationalisation.polite isnot undefined>>
	<<link [[Everything happens for a reason|$passage]]>>
	<</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if $rationalisation.money isnot undefined>>
	<<if $log[$args[0]][$args[1]][$logpars.stats].moneygain gte 500 or $log[$args[0]][$args[1]][$logpars.stats].blackmoneygain gte 5 or $log[$args[0]][$args[1]][$logpars.stats].antiquemoneygain gte 5>>
		<<link [[The money was worth it|$passage]]>>
			<<set $diary["day"+$log[$args[0]][$args[1]][$logpars.day]].entries[$entryid][3] to "The money was worth it.">>
			<<trauma -2>>
			<<set $ratiid += 1>>
		<</link>><<ltrauma>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<<if $rationalisation.pleasure isnot undefined>>
	<<if $log[$args[0]][$args[1]][$logpars.stats].arousalgain gte 5000 or $log[$args[0]][$args[1]][$logpars.stats].orgasmstatgain gte 1>>
		<<link [[At least it felt good|$passage]]>>
			<<set $diary["day"+$log[$args[0]][$args[1]][$logpars.day]].entries[$entryid][3] to "At least it felt good.">>
			<<trauma -2>>
			<<set $ratiid += 1>>
		<</link>><<ltrauma>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<<if $rationalisation.pleasing isnot undefined>>
	<<if $log[$args[0]][$args[1]][$logpars.stats].ejacstatgain gte 1>>
		<<link [[I should be happy to make others feel good|$passage]]>>
			<<set $diary["day"+$log[$args[0]][$args[1]][$logpars.day]].entries[$entryid][3] to "I should be happy to make others feel good.">>
			<<trauma -2>>
			<<set $ratiid += 1>>
		<</link>><<ltrauma>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<<if $rationalisation.defense isnot undefined>>
	<<if $log[$args[0]][$args[1]][$logpars.stats].spray gte 1 and $log[$args[0]][$args[1]][$logpars.stats].spraystatgain lte 0>>
		<<link [[I could've defended myself more if it had actually gotten bad|$passage]]>>
			<<set $diary["day"+$log[$args[0]][$args[1]][$logpars.day]].entries[$entryid][3] to "I could've defended myself more if it had actually gotten bad.">>
			<<trauma -2>>
			<<set $ratiid += 1>>
		<</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<<link [[It was horrible|$passage]]>>
<</link>>
<br>
<</capture>>

<</nobr>><</widget>>


<<widget "rationaliseinit">><<nobr>>

<<set $rationalisation to {}>>
<<set $rationalisation to {
	deserve:0,
	polite:0,
	money:0,
	plesure:0,
	pleasing:0,
	defense:0
	}>>





<</nobr>><</widget>>

<<widget "unlockrationalisation">><<nobr>>
<<if typeof($args[0]) is "string>>
	<<set $rationalisation[$args[0]] to 0>>
<<else>>
	<<run console.error("unlockrationalisation failed, " + $args[0] + " isn't a string.")>>
<</if>>

<</nobr>><</widget>>